(7783632, 1295357, 8759, '<td valign="top">
<table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kanaj:</b></div><hr/><i> I wondered if this was accomplished with a GoPro. :-) One of my higher scores in the challenge for the creativity here--and for the upending of expectations. I''m assuming that to accomplish this, you had to remain relative stationary as the subject, and the camera itself had to be in dramatic motion instead? </i></td></tr></table>
<br/>
<br/>Thank you for the comment. That is a Chinese spear (qiang). The movement is generated from the ground and through the hips, shoulders and hands to the spear itself. Hence the rotation around a fixed axle - my body. The gopro was fixed to the tip of the spear.</td>', 'Originally posted by kanaj: I wondered if this was accomplished with a GoPro. :-) One of my higher scores in the challenge for the creativity here--and for the upending of expectations. I''m assuming that to accomplish this, you had to remain relative stationary as the subject, and the camera itself had to be in dramatic motion instead? 

Thank you for the comment. That is a Chinese spear (qiang). The movement is generated from the ground and through the hips, shoulders and hands to the spear itself. Hence the rotation around a fixed axle - my body. The gopro was fixed to the tip of the spear.', '2025-06-25 06:42:02.000000', NULL, 0),
